# Cursor Rules for Langara Hacks 2025

## Performance Optimization Guidelines

### Code Splitting & Lazy Loading
- **Always use React.lazy() for below-the-fold components** that aren't immediately visible
- **Critical components** (Navigation, HeroSection, MainContent) should be imported directly
- **Non-critical components** (AboutSection, ProjectsSection, FAQSection, Footer) should be lazy loaded
- Wrap lazy components in `<Suspense>` with meaningful loading fallbacks
- Use this pattern for lazy imports:
  ```tsx
  const ComponentName = lazy(() => import('./path/to/Component.tsx').then(m => ({ default: m.ComponentName })))
  ```

### Bundle Optimization
- **Avoid barrel files** - import components directly with explicit file paths
- **Use explicit file extensions** (.tsx, .ts) for faster module resolution
- **Manual chunk splitting** should group related libraries:
  - `vendor`: React and core libraries
  - `ui`: UI component libraries  
  - `motion`: Animation libraries
  - `forms`: Form handling libraries
  - `carousel`: Carousel/slider libraries
  - `utils`: Utility libraries
- **Target modern browsers** in build config for smaller bundles

### Resource Loading
- **Preload critical resources** in index.html:
  - DNS prefetch external domains
  - Preconnect to font providers
  - Preload critical CSS and fonts
- **Use LazyImage component** for all images to enable intersection observer loading
- **Optimize images** - prefer WebP format, include proper alt text and sizes
- **Font optimization** - preload critical font files (WOFF2 format)

### Vite Configuration Best Practices
- **Use esbuild for minification** (faster than Terser)
- **Enable CSS code splitting** for better caching
- **Configure server warmup** for frequently used files during development
- **Set chunk size warning limit** to 500KB to catch bloated bundles
- **Use bundle analyzer** (`npm run build:analyze`) to monitor bundle sizes

### Import Patterns
- **NO**: `import { Component1, Component2 } from './components'` (barrel file)
- **YES**: `import { Component1 } from './components/Component1.tsx'` (direct import)
- **NO**: `import Component from './Component'` (missing extension)
- **YES**: `import Component from './Component.tsx'` (explicit extension)

### Component Architecture
- **Separate critical and non-critical components** in file organization
- **Use Suspense boundaries** strategically - don't wrap every lazy component individually if they're in the same section
- **Implement loading states** that match the design system
- **Progressive enhancement** - ensure core functionality works even if JS fails to load

### Image Optimization
- **Always use LazyImage component** instead of regular `<img>` tags
- **Include proper sizing** with `sizes` attribute for responsive images
- **Use intersection observer** for lazy loading with 50px root margin
- **Provide meaningful alt text** for accessibility
- **Optimize image formats** - WebP for photos, SVG for icons/logos

### Performance Monitoring
- **Run bundle analysis** before major releases: `npm run build:analyze`
- **Monitor bundle sizes** - main bundle should stay under 300KB
- **Check chunk distribution** - no single chunk should exceed 100KB (except vendor)
- **Test on slower connections** to verify lazy loading effectiveness

### Development Workflow
- **Use TypeScript strictly** - no `any` types, proper interface definitions
- **Explicit exports** - export named exports when possible for better tree shaking
- **Import optimization** - remove unused imports, group related imports
- **Performance first** - consider loading impact of every new dependency

### Asset Organization
- **Public assets** should be optimized and compressed
- **Static images** larger than 500KB should be reviewed for optimization
- **Font files** should be subset and converted to WOFF2
- **SVG icons** should be optimized and potentially inlined for critical icons

### Build Optimization
- **Production builds** should always be tested before deployment
- **Source maps** disabled in production for smaller file sizes
- **Modern browser targeting** to reduce polyfill overhead
- **Gzip compression** should be enabled on the server

### Code Quality
- **Use semantic HTML** for better accessibility and SEO
- **Implement proper error boundaries** around lazy-loaded content
- **Consistent loading states** across the application
- **Meaningful component names** that reflect their purpose and loading strategy

## Quick Performance Checklist
- [ ] New components below-the-fold are lazy loaded
- [ ] Imports use explicit file extensions
- [ ] No barrel file imports in critical paths
- [ ] Images use LazyImage component
- [ ] Bundle size under 300KB after adding features
- [ ] Critical resources are preloaded in HTML
- [ ] Loading states provide good user experience